// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_ship_plus_restore.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: CLAIM 6 — a band cannot share a program with an offscreen_ship fire
//          (spec §4.3).
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "offscreen_ship"
//
// EVERYTHING HERE IS INDIVIDUALLY LEGAL, which is the whole point: this is a composition
// refusal, not a malformed anything. The band is textbook — built by band(), so its two
// records carry one id and one span, CRAM $48..$4D. The shipping fire is OJZ's own shape
// (a patchable tint band declaring offscreen_ship) on palette line 3, CRAM $68..$6D,
// banded 30..60. The two spans are DISJOINT and the two line intervals are disjoint, so
// the ownership walks have nothing to say and the refusal under test is the only thing
// left that can fire.
//
// The incompatibility is about FRAME STATE, not overlap. On a shipping frame the
// frame-top DMA has already put VARIANT colours in CRAM while Palette_Ship_Snap —
// the restore's source — still holds BASE. The restore would then paint the dry
// palette over a screen the ship just made submerged.
//
// This is also what excludes Sec0 (OJZ_TwoChannel) from carrying a band, doubly: its
// channel-0 record declares offscreen_ship AND its [3,220] band leaves no legal
// interval for a second pair (spec §4.3).
//
// PARCEL-P1 NOTE. The band half is now one band() call instead of a hand-authored
// cram/restore pair: an unowned restore is refused earlier now (it carries no band id)
// and the poison would report that instead of CLAIM 6.
//
// NO IMPORTS — see poison_two_restores.emp's note.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_ship_plus_restore

const POISON_SHIP_PLUS_RESTORE = compose([
    patchable(fx_tint_band(line: 40, slot: 0, pal_line: 3, entry: 4, count: 3, sh: 0),
              ch: 0, lo: 30, hi: 60, offscreen_ship: 1),
    band(100, 140, stream_cram($48, [$0EEE, $0AAA, $0666]), 0),
])

ensure(raster_program(POISON_SHIP_PLUS_RESTORE).len > 0,
       "poison_ship_plus_restore: raster_program returned nothing — this poison no longer reaches the guard it targets")
